course: dictionary
lesson: 15900
title: A rare word: unlogical
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words start with un-, which often means not. Unhappy means not happy, and unfair means not fair. Logical means sensible and following good reasons, so unlogical means not logical.
explain: «Ben said the shop was shut, so he went there to buy bread.» His reasoning does not follow, because a shut shop cannot sell bread. Thinking like this is unlogical. Ask yourself: does the next step really follow from the one before?
explain: Unlogical is rare. Most writers and speakers use «illogical» instead, and it means exactly the same thing. When you meet unlogical, you can read it as illogical and the sentence will still make sense.
fact: Logical means following reason and good sense.
fact: Unlogical means not logical; not following reason or sense.
fact: «Unlogical» is rare. The usual everyday word is «illogical».
fact: The prefix un- often means not, as in «unhappy» and «unfair».
fact: In maths and reasoning, an illogical argument jumps to a conclusion that does not follow from the facts.
exercise: What does unlogical mean? | Happy and calm | Full of big words | *Not following reason or sense | Very neat and tidy
exercise: Which everyday word do writers usually use instead of unlogical? | *Illogical | Unhappy | Logical | Magical
exercise: «Sam said it was raining, so he took his sunhat and went out to play.» Is Sam's plan unlogical? | Yes, because it is a long walk | *Yes, the reasoning does not follow | No, it is a very kind plan | No, it is a sensible plan
test: «Her argument was unlogical, because it jumped to a conclusion that did not follow.» Which word has the same meaning as unlogical? | Quiet | *Illogical | Clever | Hopeful
test: In unlogical, what does the prefix un- mean? | *Not | Very | Before | Again
exam: Why might a writer choose illogical rather than unlogical? | Because unlogical means happy | *Because illogical is the everyday word that most people use | Because illogical is an old word that nobody understands | Because they are two different words with different meanings
